Syntax: fkeys [<path>]Function:set User-Defined Keys on VT220 TerminalsOptions: noneIf no path is given, the definitions are read from <stdin>.Syntax of key-definitions:<Function-Keynumber>=text"clear""lock"If text contains \xx, where xx is a HEX-number, the character withcode xx is taken.  \n and \t are interpreted in the same kind as 'C'. Example:fkeys .fkeyContens of File .fkey:clear11=\1b15=help\206=dir\nlockFirst the old key are cleared, then F6 is <ESC>, F15 is "help " and f6is the word "dir" followed by a <CR>.  Last the Function-keys are lockedagainst new definitions. 